course: dictionary
lesson: 11864
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and boogie is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «The whole class started to boogie when the music came on.» Here boogie is a verb: it means to dance to fast music in a fun, energetic way. «The school disco had a great boogie.» Here boogie is a noun: it means a dance.
explain: «We need to boogie, the bus is coming!» Here boogie means to move fast or leave. The clue is the bus and the hurry. Boogie is informal, so use it in chatty talk, not in formal writing.
fact: Boogie can be a verb (to dance) or a noun (a dance).
fact: «Boogie» means to dance to fast pop music in a fun, energetic way.
fact: «Boogie» can also mean to move fast or leave, as in «we need to boogie».
fact: Boogie-woogie is a style of fast blues piano music from the 1930s and 1940s.
fact: A boogie board is a short surfboard that you lie on. «Bogey» is a different word, with a different spelling and meaning.
exercise: «The whole class started to boogie when the music came on.» What does boogie mean here? | To sleep | To read quietly | *To dance in a fun, energetic way | To sing a slow song
exercise: «We need to boogie, the bus is coming!» What does boogie mean here? | To paint a picture | To stop and rest | To dance | *To move fast or leave
exercise: In «The school disco had a great boogie», what kind of word is boogie? | A word for a colour | A question word | *A noun | A verb
test: «Her big sister taught her a boogie-woogie tune on the piano.» What is boogie-woogie? | A bicycle race | A type of sandwich | *A style of fast blues piano music | A kind of cake
test: Mia says, «Bogey» means boogie. Is she right? | Yes, they both mean to run fast | Only in music lessons | *No, bogey is a different word with a different meaning | Yes, they both mean to dance
exam: «The boogie board carried Sam across the waves.» What is a boogie board? | *A short surfboard you lie on | A dance floor at a disco | A large bus | A type of piano
